# Ignore list for the VIEWER image only (viewer.Dockerfile). BuildKit prefers
# <dockerfile-path>.dockerignore over the root .dockerignore, which exists for
# the server image and excludes the TypeScript workspaces this image is made of.
#
# Same red line as everywhere else (docs/DATA-AND-LEGAL.md): nothing under
# data/ enters an image, and neither does an env file.
.git
data
node_modules
deps
docs
infra/chart
dashboard/dist
dashboard/dist-public
wrath-mcp/module
wrath-mcp/.git
.env

# Everything .gitignore keeps out of git stays out of the image: these lines
# are for a `docker build` from a working checkout. Dockerignore patterns are
# anchored at the context root where .gitignore's match at any depth, hence
# the `**/`.
**/data
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.claude
**/.wrangler
infra/fleet.json
dashboard/public/og.png
# The private reference program's place (docs/RUNBOOK.md, "The scripted
# reference run"): a build that also makes the runner image lays it in the
# context, and a viewer never carries it.
runner/src/reference
runner/test/reference
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
